backend_wire_shapes (verified against handler/model source):

  /vehicles/{id}/positions  (vehicle_handler.go:128 + vehiclePositionMappings):
    Phase-42 SI canonical projection from signal_log change feed.
    Field aliases applied by handler:  ts -> created_at, speed_mph -> speed.
    Emitted fields per row:
      latitude    (deg)
      longitude   (deg)
      heading     (deg, from GpsHeading)
      speed_mph   (m/s SI; misleadingly suffixed — VehicleSpeed normalizes to m/s
                   per internal/tesla/units/units.go:20 "speed -> meters per second")
      speed       (alias of speed_mph; same m/s SI value)
      elevation_m (meters SI)
      ts          (RFC3339 timestamp)
      created_at  (alias of ts)
      id          (synthesized from ts)
    NOT emitted: odometer, power, battery_level — frontend PositionRecord type
    declares these but they are always undefined at runtime. Pre-existing
    contract drift — preserved as graceful "—" placeholders per locked-policy
    (ADR-005 #1 do-not-delete-UI rule, same precedent as Phase-43/0023+0024+0025).

  /location-snapshots[/latest]  (location_snapshot_handler.go + locationMappings):
    Phase-42 SI canonical projection.
    Field name suffixes RETAINED for backward FE compatibility but values are SI:
      speed_mph              (m/s SI)
      miles_to_arrival       (meters SI per UnitKindDistance per
                              protomodel/signal_metadata_gen.go:1457)
      minutes_to_arrival     (minutes — UnitKindNone, no conversion)
      route_traffic_delay_min (minutes — UnitKindNone)
      elevation_m            (meters SI)
      latitude/longitude/heading                       (degrees, no conversion)
      destination_lat/destination_lon/origin_lat/origin_lon (degrees)
      destination_name, gps_state, route_last_updated  (strings)
      located_at_home, located_at_work, located_at_favorite, homelink_nearby
                                                       (booleans)

  /locations  (visited_location_handler.go + models.VisitedLocation):
    Snake-case fields: id, vehicle_id, address_id, address_name, visit_count,
    total_duration_min (float minutes), last_visited (nullable RFC3339),
    created_at. NO unit conversion required.

  /geofences  (geofence_handler.go + models.Geofence + MarshalJSON augmentation):
    Backend struct fields:
      id (int64), name (string), polygon_wkt (string), category (nullable string),
      created_at, updated_at (RFC3339)
    MarshalJSON adds derived:
      latitude, longitude (degrees, polygon centroid),
      radius (meters, max-vertex-distance from centroid)
    NOT emitted by backend (NEVER were since the post-migration schema):
      enabled, alert_on_entry, alert_on_exit, cost_per_kwh
    Pre-existing contract drift — see GeofencesPage_field_drift below.

  /analytics/temperature-impact  (temp_impact_handler.go):
    Response shape: { points, efficiency, vampire_drain (always []), monthly_trend }
    Per-point fields: outside_temp (°C SI from ambient_temp_c_avg),
                      efficiency_wh_km (Wh/km derived in SQL),
                      distance_km (km derived in SQL: distance_m / 1000.0),
                      drive_date (YYYY-MM-DD).

frontend_type_alignment_assessment:
  web/src/api/types.ts has snake-case authoritative types regenerated in
  prompt 0011: VisitedLocation (api/types.ts:1070) and Geofence
  (api/types.ts:206). The legacy web/src/types/location.ts module
  declares camelCase Location (id:string, addressName, visitCount,
  totalDurationMin, lastVisited) and Geofence (id:string, alertOnEntry,
  alertOnExit, enabled, costPerKwh, createdAt) — neither matches the
  backend wire shape exactly.

useLocations_hook_type_migration_deferral:
  The prompt asks to update useLocations.ts return type to use the
  matching api/types.ts interface. Doing so would cascade type errors
  into the following OUT-OF-SCOPE consumer files (not in allowed_files):
    web/src/features/dashboard/widgets/LocationFavoritesWidget.tsx
      uses loc.addressName, loc.visitCount, loc.lastVisited (camelCase)
    web/src/features/dashboard/widgets/GeofenceWidget.tsx
      uses f.enabled (field never emitted by backend; closest map: derived
      from input geofence to the f mapper which propagates `enabled` from
      the legacy type — would TS-fail under the new Geofence type)
    web/src/features/automations/pages/TriggerConfigurator.tsx
      uses g.id (number ok), g.name — backward compatible with new type
    web/src/features/automations/pages/ConditionBuilder.tsx
      uses g.id (number ok), g.name — backward compatible
    web/src/features/vehicle-systems/pages/GuardModePage.tsx
      uses g.id (number ok), g.name — backward compatible
  Per locked-policy precedent (Phase-43/0026 BE/FE Trip mismatch
  deferral, Phase-43/0024 useSignalCatalog deprecation, Phase-43/0023
  vampire-drain deferral): keep the hook return types pointing at the
  legacy @/types/location module to preserve TS-compile across all
  consumers, and add JSDoc @deprecated notes so future audits can
  reconcile the camelCase legacy module against api/types.ts in a
  separate prompt that is allowed to touch dashboard widgets.
  The hooks' URLs and snake_case query params already conform.

GeofencesPage_field_drift:
  GeofencesPage references g.enabled, g.alertOnEntry, g.alertOnExit,
  g.costPerKwh, g.createdAt — none of which the backend has emitted
  since the post-migration schema (models.Geofence in
  internal/models/system.go:89 has only id, name, polygon_wkt, category,
  created_at, updated_at; MarshalJSON adds latitude, longitude, radius).
  This is a long-standing pre-existing UI bug: toggle switches always
  read "Inactive", entry/exit alert badges always read "None", cost-per-
  kWh inputs always start blank. The bug predates Phase-43 and is not
  introduced by this prompt. Per ADR-005 #1 (do not delete UI), the
  page is preserved as-is. STATUS=BLOCKED is NOT triggered because the
  contract drift is not new and not introduced by Phase-43; reconciling
  it requires a backend migration to add enable/alert columns plus a
  separate prompt that can touch internal/models/system.go +
  internal/api/geofence_handler.go + this page in lockstep.

