1. LOCKED-POLICY DEFERRAL of useLocations / useGeofences type unification:
   The prompt asked to repoint hook return types at api/types.ts. Doing so
   would TS-fail 5 out-of-scope consumer files (LocationFavoritesWidget,
   GeofenceWidget, TriggerConfigurator, ConditionBuilder, GuardModePage)
   that read camelCase fields and the missing enabled/alertOn*/costPerKwh.
   Per Phase-43/0023 (vampire-drain), /0024 (signal-catalog), /0025
   (mileage-stats x4), /0026 (useTrip(id)) precedent: keep the legacy
   type imports + add @deprecated JSDoc explaining the deferral. Future
   reconciliation needs a prompt that can touch the dashboard widgets
   AND legacy types in lockstep.

2. PRE-EXISTING BACKEND FIELD DRIFT in GeofencesPage:
   g.enabled / g.alertOnEntry / g.alertOnExit / g.costPerKwh are read by
   the page but the backend models.Geofence (system.go:89) has never
   emitted them post-migration. This is long-standing UI bug — toggle
   switches always read "Inactive", entry/exit alert badges always read
   "None", cost-per-kWh inputs always start blank. Bug predates Phase-43;
   not introduced by this prompt. STATUS=BLOCKED is NOT triggered because
   the contract drift is not new. Reconciling requires a backend migration
   to add the missing columns plus a coordinated prompt that can touch
   internal/models/system.go + internal/api/geofence_handler.go + this
   page in lockstep.

3. PRE-EXISTING DISPLAY BUG FIXED in NavigationRoutePage:
   Legacy code applied useSettings.convertDistance to s.miles_to_arrival.
   Since Phase-42 SI normalize routes the value to meters (despite the
   misleading legacy field name), the legacy converter was scaling
   meters as if they were miles, producing 1609x inflated output.
   convertDistanceFromSI(meters, distanceUnit) now yields the correct
   "10 km" / "6.2 mi" value. Same fix for waypointColumns.

4. PRE-EXISTING DISPLAY BUG NOT FIXED (out of scope) in MapOverviewPage:
   latest.odometer is declared on PositionRecord but never emitted by
   /vehicles/{id}/positions (vehiclePositionMappings projects only
   Latitude, Longitude, GpsHeading, VehicleSpeed, Elevation). At runtime
   it's always undefined, so the panel renders '—'. Fixing requires
   adding Odometer to the vehiclePositionMappings projection, which is a
   backend change outside the allowed_files boundary. Same applies to
   latest.battery_level / latest.power.

5. NO convertEfficiencyFromSI helper exists in lib/unitConversion.ts
   (per Phase-43/0025 precedent). TemperatureImpactPage keeps the inline
   KM_PER_MILE = 1.609344 module-level constant for Wh/km -> Wh/mi
   conversion. A future helper consolidation prompt could add
   convertEfficiencyFromSI(whPerKm, 'Wh/km' | 'Wh/mi').

6. LocationsPage.tsx and GeofencesPage.tsx have ZERO net code changes —
   no SI conversion is appropriate for their fields (visit_count,
   total_duration_min, geofence radius rendered as literal '{value}m').
   The pages are preserved per ADR-005 #1.

